---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import { BUSINESS, LAST_UPDATED } from "../lib/site";
---

<Page
  title="Cancellation and refunds | Waymark"
  description="Your cancellation rights and how refunds work for Waymark purchases."
  heading="Cancellation and refunds"
  updated={LAST_UPDATED}
>
  <p class="note">Payments are not open yet. This page describes how refunds will work at launch.</p>

  <h2>Your right to cancel</h2>
  <p>
    UK law usually gives you 14 days to cancel an online purchase. For digital content you can use straight away, that
    right ends once you agree to start using it. At checkout we will ask you to tick a box confirming that you want
    access to start immediately and that you understand you lose the right to cancel. We will never tick it for you.
  </p>

  <h2>If there's a problem</h2>
  <p>
    If Waymark doesn't work as described, or content is faulty, tell us at
    <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.support}`}>{BUSINESS.support}</a>. We will fix it and, where the law requires it or
    the problem can't be fixed, refund you.
  </p>

  <h2>Pass promise</h2>
  <p>
    Separately from your legal rights, we plan to offer a <a href="/pass-promise">pass promise</a>. Its terms will be
    published before it applies to any purchase.
  </p>

  <h2>How refunds are paid</h2>
  <p>Refunds go back to the card you paid with, usually within 5–10 working days of approval.</p>
</Page>
